{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/902630-sprinting","id":902630,"title":"Sprinting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-29T05:03:41-07:00","id":902630,"title":"Sprinting","content":"Can no one sprint in 2E? There were rules for it previously (moving up to 2x speed, I think) but I can't find any reference in any 2E books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T05:09:21-07:00","id":902632,"title":"","content":"Its possible that it was just an oversight, given how the GMC were originally a hack to the 1e rulebook, and then CofD rulebook came out... but its also just possible that its not necessary. Sprinting only causes headahces through unnecessary complecations when it comes to Chase rules, and its really never come up for me in the middle of combat. I've never seen sprinting being necessary anywhere else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T05:12:54-07:00","id":902633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/902630-sprinting?p=902632#post902632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its possible that it was just an oversight, given how the GMC were originally a hack to the 1e rulebook, and then CofD rulebook came out... but its also just possible that its not necessary. Sprinting only causes headahces through unnecessary complecations when it comes to Chase rules, and its really never come up for me in the middle of combat. I've never seen sprinting being necessary anywhere else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm totally okay for the rule being gone, but there's an Atavism that refers to it in the Beast book, but there's no actual rules for it on the page number referenced. I tried to look for it in the other books, but nothing.<br /> <br /> Edit: I should be fine using 2x for lingering references, right? That's what a Charge lets you move.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 05-29-2016, 08:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T05:28:42-07:00","id":902640,"title":"","content":"Huh. Sprint was never an official term in the WoD rules. Well, anyways, yes, double speed sounds about right here, given the context of the Wings of the Raptor power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T07:14:16-07:00","id":902697,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronciles-world-of-darkness?p=887758#post887758\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...758#post887758</a><br /> <br /> <br /> Starting from here, we had a discussion of the running rules.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Page 92 of the CoD corebook<br /> <br /> Movement<br /> A character can move his Speed in a single turn and still<br /> take an instant action. He can give up his action to move at<br /> double his normal Speed.&quot;<br /> Courtesy of Fumus<br /> <br /> Also, you can perform a charge action which is double the base move speed and an attack at the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T08:10:11-07:00","id":902723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/902630-sprinting?p=902697#post902697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronciles-world-of-darkness?p=887758#post887758\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...758#post887758</a><br /> <br /> <br /> Starting from here, we had a discussion of the running rules.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Page 92 of the CoD corebook<br /> <br /> Movement<br /> A character can move his Speed in a single turn and still<br /> take an instant action. He can give up his action to move at<br /> double his normal Speed.&quot;<br /> Courtesy of Fumus<br /> <br /> Also, you can perform a charge action which is double the base move speed and an attack at the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}